{"name":"Night Fog","hex":"#2d1962","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Variable spellings of night in a Middle English poem:\n\nÞu sittest a dai & fliȝst a niȝt (top)\nÞu sittest a day and flyhst a niht (bottom)\n'You sit by day and fly by night'\n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOwl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/1280px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Day and night during the winter solstice in the northern hemisphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/500px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/1280px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/500px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The drainage basin of the Nile River and delta at night","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/MarsSunset.jpg/500px-MarsSunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/MarsSunset.jpg/1280px-MarsSunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/MarsSunset.jpg/500px-MarsSunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum